  m_Name: EllipsePolygonsInfo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WorkshopExampleInfo
  m_Scene: {fileID: 102900000, guid: f596a2ba3399b58458c8fa9e558ddf4e, type: 3}
  m_ScenePath: Assets/Examples/EllipsePolygons/EllipsePolygons.unity
  m_ExampleName: Ellipse Polygons
  m_Category: Shapes
  m_Purpose: "Demonstrates approximating an ellipse, which has no shape of its own, with a rounded polygon. A thin polygon with a radius rounds into a smooth oval.\nIt also shows how stable a complex stack of rounded polygons is. A grid of these shapes falls on top of each other into a tall box and settles until the bodies sleep. Disturb the pile and it collapses and settles again correctly."
  m_Controls: "Column Count and Row Count: the size of the grid.\nFriction and Restitution: the friction and the bounciness of every shape.\nThe grid is dropped again when any of them changes."
  m_Description: Demonstrating creating pseudo-ellipse shapes as Polygons.
